    <div class="row">
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <div class="custom-slider">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Width</p>
                <input id="widthSlider" type="range" class="ap-slider" min="100" max="300" value="150" step="1"
                       oninput="widthChanged()"/>
                <label id="widthLabel" for="widthSlider">Width: 150px</label><br>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <div class="custom-slider">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Height</p>
                <input id="heightSlider" type="range" class="ap-slider" min="30" max="64" value="30" step="1"
                       oninput="heightChanged()"/>
                <label id="heightLabel" for="heightSlider">Height: 30px</label><br>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <div class="custom-slider">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Corner Radius</p>
                <input id="radiusSlider" type="range" class="ap-slider" min="0" max="100" value="3" step="1"
                       oninput="radiusChanged()"/>
                <label id="radiusLabel" for="radiusSlider">Corner Radius: 3px</label><br>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <div class="custom-slider">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Padding Y</p>
                <input id="paddingYSlider" type="range" class="ap-slider" min="0" max="32" value="0" step="1"
                       oninput="paddingChanged()"/>
                <label id="paddingYLabel" for="paddingYSlider">Button Padding Y: 0px</label><br>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <div class="custom-slider">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Padding X</p>
                <input id="paddingXSlider" type="range" class="ap-slider" min="0" max="32" value="0" step="1"
                       oninput="paddingChanged()"/>
                <label id="paddingXLabel" for="paddingXSlider">Button Padding X: 0px</label><br>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="column column-padded-r large-4 medium-4 small-12">
            <span class="custom-dropdown">
                <p class="dropdown-label">Button Box Sizing</p>
                <select class="applePayButtonConfig apd-dropdown"
                        id="boxSizing" onchange="boxSizingChanged()">
                    <option value="border-box" selected="">Border Box</option>
                    <option value="content-box">Content Box</option>
                </select>
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <pre class="prettyprint">
&lt;style&gt;
apple-pay-button {
  --apple-pay-button-width: <span id="widthChange">150</span>px;
  --apple-pay-button-height: <span id="heightChange">30</span>px;
  --apple-pay-button-border-radius: <span id="radiusChange">3</span>px;
  --apple-pay-button-padding: <span id="paddingYChange">0</span>px <span id="paddingXChange">0</span>px;
  --apple-pay-button-box-sizing: <span id="boxSizingChange">border-box</span>;
}
&lt;/style&gt;
&lt;apple-pay-button buttonstyle="<span
            id="buttonstyleChange">black</span>" type="<span
            id="typeChange">plain</span>" locale="<span
            id="localeChange">en-US</span>"&gt;&lt;/apple-pay-button&gt;
</pre>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2 id="createAPayment">Create a Payment Request</h2>
    <p>When your customer clicks or taps the Apple&nbsp;Pay button, you construct a <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentrequest-interface"
            target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentRequest</code></a>.</p>
    <br>
    <pre class="prettyprint">
var request = null;
if (window.PaymentRequest)
    request = new PaymentRequest(methods, details, options);
else
    // Consider using Apple Pay JS instead.
</pre>
    <br>
    <p>
        The <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentrequest-interface" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentRequest</code></a> constructor takes three arguments:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>The payment methods you support</li>
        <li>The details to show to your customer (like shipping options and total amount)</li>
        <li>The options you require</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Payment methods</h3>
    <p>
        Payment methods represent the means by which you can accept payments from your customer using the
        Payment Request API. You specify the payment methods you accept as a sequence of <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentmethoddata-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentMethodData</code></a> dictionaries, each of which contains an identifier (<a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentmethoddata-supportedmethods" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">supportedMethods</code></a>) and associated information (<a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentmethoddata-data" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">data</code></a>).
    </p>
    <p>
        To accept payments using Apple Pay through the Payment Request API, include it as a payment method. Apple Pay&rsquo;s
        <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-method-id/#url-based-payment-method-identifiers"
           target="_blank">URL-based</a> payment method identifier is <code class="inline-code">"https://apple.com/apple-pay"</code>,
        and its associated <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentmethoddata-data"
                              target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">data</code></a> is an <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepayrequest"
            target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">ApplePayRequest</code></a> dictionary.
    </p>
    <p>
        Safari supports only the Apple Pay payment method. Other browsers may support additional methods. The system
        determines which payment methods to present based on the capabilities of the device and on user
        preferences when specifying more than one method.
    </p>
    <h4>Try it: Apple Pay method</h4>
    <p>
        You may configure the values in the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentmethoddata-dictionary"
            target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentMethodData</code></a> structure below.
    </p>
    <p>
        Select &ldquo;Basic request&rdquo; to see a payment sheet with only the required fields.
        Select &ldquo;Detailed request&rdquo; to include optional fields.
    </p>
    <p>
        Click or tap the Apple Pay button below to see how the payment sheet displays information.
    </p>
    <div class="form-table">
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="A" type="radio" name="PaymentMethodData" id="PaymentMethodDataA"
                   checked="checked"
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentMethodDataA">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Basic payment request (required fields only)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="B" type="radio" name="PaymentMethodData" id="PaymentMethodDataB"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentMethodDataB">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Detailed payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodeEmpty" type="radio" name="PaymentMethodData" id="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodeEmpty"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodeEmpty">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Empty coupon code payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodePercentOff" type="radio" name="PaymentMethodData" id="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodePercentOff"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodePercentOff">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> 20% off coupon code payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodeFreeShipping" type="radio" name="PaymentMethodData" id="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodeFreeShipping"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentMethodDataCouponCodeFreeShipping">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Free shipping coupon code payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <div class="jsoneditor" id="PaymentMethodData"></div>
    <br>
    <h3>Payment details</h3>
    <p>Supply the payment details in the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentdetailsinit-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentDetailsInit</code></a> dictionary. It contains your transaction&rsquo;s total amount,
        display items, shipping options, and payment method-specific modifiers.
    </p>
    <p>Select a default shipping option by setting the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentshippingoption-selected" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">selected</code></a> attribute to <code class="inline-code">true</code> as this demo
        shows in <a href="#tryItPaymentDetails">Try it: Payment details</a> for <code class="inline-code">"Ground
        Shipping"</code> when selecting &ldquo;More details&ldquo;. The total amount needs to be $0.00 or greater,
        and when using Apple&nbsp;Pay, all payment amounts in your request need to use the same <a
                href="https://www.iso.org/iso-4217-currency-codes.html" target="_blank">ISO 4217 currency code</a>.
        It&rsquo;s your responsibility to ensure the correctness of your payment details; Safari doesn&rsquo;t perform any
        currency calculations on your behalf.
    </p>
    <h4 id="paymentModifiers">Payment modifiers</h4>
    <p>
        Apple Pay can update your transaction&rsquo;s display items and total when you include optional <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentdetailsbase-modifiers" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">modifiers</code></a> in your payment details. For example, you can adjust the price
        based on the type of payment card.
    </p>
    <p>Modifiers provide some of the functionality present in the
        <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaysession/onpaymentmethodselected"
           target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">paymentmethodselected</code></a> event. For more information, see
        <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier" target="_blank"><code
                class="inline-code">ApplePayModifier</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can set up recurring payments, such as subscriptions, that feature different payment intervals (such as
        annually or monthly) and billing cycles (such as regular or trial) by passing <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier/recurringpaymentrequest" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">recurringPaymentRequest</code></a> to the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayModifier</code></a> with the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayLineItem</code></a> that has a <code class="inline-code">recurring</code> <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/paymenttiming" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">paymentTiming</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can set up deferred payments, where a user pays at a later date, by passing <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayLineItem</code></a> that has a <code class="inline-code">recurring</code> <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/paymenttiming" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">paymentTiming</code></a> and a valid date in the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/deferredpaymentdate" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">deferredPaymentDate</code></a> property in the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayModifier</code></a> <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier/additionallineitems"
            target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">additionalLineItems</code></a>.
    </p>
    <p>
        You can set up automatic reload payments, such as store card top-ups, by passing <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepayautomaticreloadpaymentrequest" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">automaticReloadPaymentRequest</code></a> to the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayModifier</code></a> with the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayLineItem</code></a> that has an <code class="inline-code">automaticReload</code> <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/paymenttiming" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">paymentTiming</code></a>,
            the <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/amount" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">amount</code></a>
            to describe the reload amount, and the
            <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaylineitem/automaticreloadpaymentthresholda" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">automaticReloadPaymentThresholdAmount</code></a>
            to describe the threshold amount balance to reach before automatically applying the reload amount.
    </p>
    <aside aria-label="note" class="aside aside-important">
    <p class="aside-name">Note</p>
    
    <p>
        You must also include <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepayautomaticreloadpaymentrequest/managementurl" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">managementURL</code></a>,
        the URL where the user can update or delete the payment method for the automatic payment, and
        <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepayautomaticreloadpaymentrequest/tokennotificationurl" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">tokenNotificationURL</code></a>,
        an API endpoint on your web service that receives life-cycle notifications from Apple Pay servers about the
        Apple&nbsp;Pay merchant token for the recurring payment. See
        <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/merchanttokennotificationservices" target="_blank">Apple Pay Merchant Token Management API</a>
        for more details about implementing and interacting with merchant tokens APIs.
    </p>
    
</aside>
    <p>
        You can set up multitoken transactions to process and display payments with multiple merchants on one payment
        sheet, such as a booking site where a user pays for a hotel, a flight, and a car rental from different
        merchants in a single Apple&nbsp;Pay transaction. You can do this by passing <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaypaymenttokencontext" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">ApplePayPaymentTokenContext</code></a> in the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier/multitokencontexts" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">multiTokenContexts</code></a> property to the <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaymodifier target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">ApplePayModifier</code></a>.
    </p>
    <h4 id="tryItPaymentDetails">Try it: Payment details</h4>
    <p>
        Modify the values in the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentdetailsinit-dictionary"
            target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentDetailsInit</code></a> structure below
        and click or tap the Apple Pay button to view the payment sheet.
    </p>
    <div class="form-table">
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="A" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsA"
                   checked="checked"
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsA">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Basic details
            </label>
            
            (required fields only)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="B" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsB"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsB">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> More details
            </label>
            
            (includes optional fields)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="C" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsC"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsC">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> More details with modifiers
            </label>
            
            (includes a payment modifier that adds a $1.00 discount for using a debit card)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodeEmpty" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsCouponCodeEmpty"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsCouponCodeEmpty">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Empty coupon code payment
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodePercentOff" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsCouponCodePercentOff"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsCouponCodePercentOff">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> 20% off coupon code payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="CouponCodeFreeShipping" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsCouponCodeFreeShipping"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsCouponCodeFreeShipping">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Free shipping coupon code payment request
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="D" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsD"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsD">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Recurring payment request
            </label>
            
            (includes a payment modifier that creates a recurring subscription payment request)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="F" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsF"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsF">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Deferred payment
            </label>
            
            (includes a payment modifier that creates a deferred, future date payment)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="G" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsG"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsG">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Automatic reload payment
            </label>
            
            (includes a payment modifier that creates an automatic reload payment request)
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="E" type="radio" name="PaymentDetails" id="PaymentDetailsE"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsE">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Multimerchant payment
            </label>
            
            (creates a combined airline and hotel payment transaction using a modifier with multiple payment tokens
            by passing one context for each token)
            <aside aria-label="note" class="aside aside-important">
    <p class="aside-name">Note</p>
    
            <p>
            Only select credit and debit cards support multimerchant payments at this time.<br/>
            If your card doesn&rsquo;t support multimerchant payments, the payment sheet indicates that this
            website doesn&rsquo;t accept the selected payment card.
            </p>
            
</aside>
        
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <div class="jsoneditor" id="PaymentDetails"></div>
    <br>
    <h3>Payment options</h3>
    <p>
        Use <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentoptions-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentOptions</code></a> to specify the information to request from your customer.
        You can request your customer&rsquo;s name, email address, or phone number, or request a certain type of shipping.
    </p>
    <h4>Try it: Payment Options</h4>
    <p>
        You may configure the values in the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentoptions-dictionary"
                                               target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentOptions</code></a>
        structure below.
    </p>
    <p>
        Select &rdquo;Request no additional information&rdquo; to see a payment sheet with no customer data requests.
        Select &rdquo;Request shipping information&rdquo; to see a payment sheet with only a shipping request.
        Select &rdquo;Request all information&rdquo; to see a payment sheet with all customer data requests.
    </p>
    <p>
        Click or tap the Apple Pay button to see how the payment sheet displays information.
    </p>
    <div class="form-table">
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="A" type="radio" name="PaymentOptions" id="PaymentOptionsA"
                   checked="checked"
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentOptionsA">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Request no additional information
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="B" type="radio" name="PaymentOptions" id="PaymentOptionsB"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentOptionsB">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Request shipping information
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="C" type="radio" name="PaymentOptions" id="PaymentOptionsC"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentOptionsC">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Request all information
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <div class="jsoneditor" id="PaymentOptions"></div>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2 id="merchantValidation">Complete merchant validation</h2>
    <p>
        Before you are able to display the payment sheet to the customer, you need to generate a valid payment session by
        interacting with Apple Pay servers. For security reasons, your server needs to do this interaction, not your browser client
        code, unlike everything else in this demo. To start the merchant validation process, call the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#show-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">show</code></a> method on the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentrequest-interface" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentRequest</code></a> you created above.
    </p>
    <p>
        After calling the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#show-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">show</code></a> method, the browser invokes your <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/merchant-validation/" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">onmerchantvalidation</code></a> handler, which needs to fetch a merchant session from your
        server.
    </p>
    <p>
        Refer to the instructions in <a
            href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/requesting-an-apple-pay-payment-session"
            target="_blank">Requesting an Apple&nbsp;Pay Payment Session</a> to implement your server endpoint
        responsible for fetching the merchant session object from Apple Pay servers. If the fetch is successful, Apple Pay servers
        return a merchant session object, which your server needs to then pass back as the response to the browser.
    </p>
    <p>
        You need to complete your <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/merchant-validation/#onmerchantvalidation-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">onmerchantvalidation</code></a> handler by passing the promise, containing the merchant
        session response, to the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/merchant-validation/#complete-method"
                                   target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">complete</code></a> method on the event.
        The browser then displays the payment sheet.
    </p>
    <p>
        The following code shows an example of how to validate a merchant to generate a payment session:
    </p>
    <br>
    <pre class="prettyprint">
request.onmerchantvalidation = event => {
    // Call your own server to request a new merchant session.
    const merchantSessionPromise = fetch("/authorizeMerchant")
        .then(res => res.json()) // Parse the response as JSON.
        .catch(err => {
            console.error("Error fetching merchant session", err);
        });

    event.complete(merchantSessionPromise);
};
</pre>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2 id="paymentSheetInteractions">Respond to payment sheet interactions</h2>
    <p>
        After merchant validation is complete, Apple Pay provides the information about your customer&rsquo;s payment sheet
        selections so that you can calculate the final transaction cost. The final details of a transaction may depend
        on the user&rsquo;s payment method, shipping address and method, or any coupons the user enters.
        To handle these adjustments, implement the optional handlers <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#onpaymentmethodchange-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">onpaymentmethodchange</code></a>, <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#onshippingoptionchange-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">onshippingoptionchange</code></a>, and <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#onshippingaddresschange-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">onshippingaddresschange</code></a>.
        In the event handlers, you can determine the user&rsquo;s selection using the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentrequest-interface" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentRequest</code></a> <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#shippingoption-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">shippingOption</code></a> and <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#shippingaddress-attribute" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">shippingAddress</code></a> attributes.
    </p>
    <p>
        When the browser calls one of these handlers, you need to call the event object&rsquo;s <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#updatewith-method" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">updateWith</code></a>
        callback function with a promise that resolves within 30 seconds to a <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentdetailsupdate-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentDetailsUpdate</code></a>; otherwise, the transaction times out.
    </p>
    <aside aria-label="note" class="aside aside-important">
    <p class="aside-name">Note</p>
    
    <p>
        To ensure that the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentdetailsbase-displayitems" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">displayItems</code></a> and the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentdetailsbase-modifiers" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">modifiers</code></a> don&rsquo;t reset, you need to pass them to the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentdetailsupdate-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentDetailsUpdate</code></a>.
    </p>
    
</aside>
    <h3 id="shippingAddressSelection">Request a shipping address</h3>
    <p>
        If you set <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentoptions-requestshipping"
                      target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">requestShipping</code></a> to <code
            class="inline-code">true</code> in the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentoptions-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentOptions</code></a> dictionary, Apple Pay provides redacted address information
        before the user authenticates the transaction. After the user authenticates, Apple Pay provides the full contact
        information in the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentresponse-interface"
                              target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentResponse</code></a> that the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#show-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">show</code></a> method&rsquo;s returned promise resolves.
    </p>
    <p>
        The redacted payment information includes only the data necessary to complete
        required transaction tasks, such as calculating taxes or shipping costs, and may
        differ based on the user&rsquo;s geographic region.
    </p>
    <p>
        The following code shows an example of redacted payment information:
    </p>
    <br>
    <pre class="prettyprint">
shippingAddress:
{
    "administrativeArea": "CA",
    "country": "United States",
    "countryCode": "US",
    "familyName": "",
    "givenName": "",
    "locality": "San Francisco",
    "phoneticFamilyName": "",
    "phoneticGivenName": "",
    "postalCode": "94114",
    "subAdministrativeArea": "",
    "subLocality": ""
}
</pre>
    <br>
    <h4>Try it: Updating payment details</h4>
    <p>
        You may customize the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentdetailsupdate-dictionary"
                                 target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentDetailsUpdate</code></a> below.
    </p>
    <p>
        Select one of the Success options below (with or without updating display items and total) to see a successful response.
        Select Failure to see response with custom errors.
    </p>
    <p>
        Click or tap the Apple Pay button to see how the payment sheet displays updates or address errors.
    </p>
    <div class="form-table">
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="A" type="radio" name="PaymentDetailsUpdate" id="PaymentDetailsUpdateA"
                   checked="checked"
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsUpdateA">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Success (no update)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="B" type="radio" name="PaymentDetailsUpdate" id="PaymentDetailsUpdateB"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsUpdateB">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Success (update display items and total)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="C" type="radio" name="PaymentDetailsUpdate" id="PaymentDetailsUpdateC"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsUpdateC">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Success (update modifiers with additional shipping method)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="D" type="radio" name="PaymentDetailsUpdate" id="PaymentDetailsUpdateD"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsUpdateD">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Failure (shipping address error)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="E" type="radio" name="PaymentDetailsUpdate" id="PaymentDetailsUpdateE"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentDetailsUpdateE">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Failure (payer error)
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <div class="jsoneditor" id="PaymentDetailsUpdate"></div>
    <br>
    <h3 id="authorizingThePayment">Authorize the payment</h3>
    <p>
        Finally, you receive a <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentresponse-interface"
                                  target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">PaymentResponse</code></a> through the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#show-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">show</code></a> method&rsquo;s returned promise to process the
        transaction. After the user authenticates the transaction using Face ID, Touch ID, or their
        device passcode, this promise resolves with the encrypted Apple Pay token, as well as any fields you request
        in the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#paymentoptions-dictionary" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">PaymentOptions</code></a>. To finalize the transaction, you need to pass the encrypted
        payment token to your payment processor using their API.
    </p>
    <p>
        After you receive the response from your payment processor, call the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#complete-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">complete</code></a> method on the response and pass in a status of <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentcomplete-success" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">success</code></a> or <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentcomplete-fail"><code
            class="inline-code">fail</code></a>.
    </p>
    <aside aria-label="note" class="aside aside-important">
    <p class="aside-name">Note</p>
    
        <p>Starting with iOS 16 and macOS 13, you can send an additional
            <a href="https://developer.apple.com/documentation/applepayontheweb/applepaypaymentcompletedetails" target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">ApplePayPaymentCompleteDetails</code></a>
            argument to the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#complete-method" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">complete</code></a> handler. This payload includes order
            information that will be visible on users&rsquo; devices.</p>
        <p>It&rsquo;s safe to send this additional argument for older OS versions &mdash; it just doesn&rsquo;t
            process unless the user is using a recent OS.</p>
        <p>See the <a href="/order-tracking/payment-request-api">Order Tracking</a> demo for details.</p>
    
</aside>
    <p>
        You may also validate the user&rsquo;s information, and invoke the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#complete-method"><code
            class="inline-code">complete</code></a> method immediately, without calling the payment processor, if you
        detect a problem with the selected options (for example, if the user selects a shipping address in a
        location that you don&rsquo;t service).
    </p>
    <p>
        The following code shows an example of passing a status to the <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#complete-method">
        <code class="inline-code">complete</code></a> method:
    </p>
    <br>
    <pre class="prettyprint">
const response = await request.show();
const status = "success";
await response.complete(status);
    </pre>
    <br>
    <h4>Try it: Complete the payment</h4>
    <p>
        You may customize the <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#complete-method"
            target="_blank"><code class="inline-code">complete</code></a> response
        below.
    </p>
    <p>
        Select Success to default to <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentcomplete-success" target="_blank"><code
            class="inline-code">success</code></a>. Select Failure to see a <a
            href="https://www.w3.org/TR/payment-request/#dom-paymentcomplete-fail"><code
            class="inline-code">fail</code></a> response.
    </p>
    <p>
        Click or tap the Apple Pay button to see how the payment sheet completes the payment.
    </p>
    <div class="form-table">
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="A" type="radio" name="PaymentComplete" id="PaymentCompleteA"
                   checked="checked"
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentCompleteA">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Success
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
        <div class="form-row">
    <div class="form-cell">
        <div class="form-element">
            <input value="B" type="radio" name="PaymentComplete" id="PaymentCompleteB"
                   
                   class="choosePreset form-choice form-choice-radio" onchange="presetChanged()">
            <label class="form-label" for="PaymentCompleteB">
                <span class="form-choice-indicator"></span> Failure
            </label>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
    </div>
    <br>
    <div class="jsoneditor" id="PaymentComplete"></div>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <h2>Disbursements</h2>
    <p>
        Implement the <a href="/disbursement-request-api#createADisbursement">Disbursement Request API</a> to disburse funds to your customer.
        With the Disbursement Request API, you can allow your site visitors to transfer funds from your site to an account that is linked
        to a card in Wallet. The Disbursement Request API is only available as a subset of the Payment Request API.
    </p>
</section>
                        
                    
                </div>
